1. the build from scratch
% python make.py -C project
plan: 6 targets
  main.o    <- main.c shape.h vec.h       cc  -O2 -Wall -c main.c -o main.o
  report.o  <- report.c vec.h             cc  -O2 -Wall -c report.c -o report.o
  vec.o     <- vec.c vec.h                cc  -O2 -Wall -c vec.c -o vec.o
  shape.o   <- shape.c shape.h vec.h      cc  -O2 -Wall -c shape.c -o shape.o
  libgeom.a <- vec.o shape.o              ar rcs libgeom.a vec.o shape.o
  demo      <- main.o report.o libgeom.a  cc -o demo main.o report.o libgeom.a
waves: [main.o report.o vec.o shape.o] [libgeom.a] [demo]
cc  -O2 -Wall -c main.c -o main.o
cc  -O2 -Wall -c report.c -o report.o
cc  -O2 -Wall -c vec.c -o vec.o
cc  -O2 -Wall -c shape.c -o shape.o
ar rcs libgeom.a vec.o shape.o
cc -o demo main.o report.o libgeom.a
% project/demo
c = (0, 3)
area = 6

2. build again: nothing to do
% python make.py -C project
plan: nothing to do

3. touch shape.h: the inverse query, then the rebuild
% python make.py -C project --touch shape.h --affected shape.h
affected: demo libgeom.a main.o shape.o
plan: 4 targets
  main.o    <- main.c shape.h vec.h       cc  -O2 -Wall -c main.c -o main.o
  shape.o   <- shape.c shape.h vec.h      cc  -O2 -Wall -c shape.c -o shape.o
  libgeom.a <- vec.o shape.o              ar rcs libgeom.a vec.o shape.o
  demo      <- main.o report.o libgeom.a  cc -o demo main.o report.o libgeom.a
waves: [main.o shape.o] [libgeom.a] [demo]
cc  -O2 -Wall -c main.c -o main.o
cc  -O2 -Wall -c shape.c -o shape.o
ar rcs libgeom.a vec.o shape.o
cc -o demo main.o report.o libgeom.a

4. DEBUG=1: the command line replaces the assignment, and the recipes change
% python make.py -C fresh DEBUG=1 -n
plan: 6 targets
  main.o    <- main.c shape.h vec.h       cc  -O0 -g -Wall -c main.c -o main.o
  report.o  <- report.c vec.h             cc  -O0 -g -Wall -c report.c -o report.o
  vec.o     <- vec.c vec.h                cc  -O0 -g -Wall -c vec.c -o vec.o
  shape.o   <- shape.c shape.h vec.h      cc  -O0 -g -Wall -c shape.c -o shape.o
  libgeom.a <- vec.o shape.o              ar rcs libgeom.a vec.o shape.o
  demo      <- main.o report.o libgeom.a  cc -o demo main.o report.o libgeom.a
waves: [main.o report.o vec.o shape.o] [libgeom.a] [demo]

5. WITH_PLOT=1: plot.o joins the library, the define, one line more
% python make.py -C plot WITH_PLOT=1
plan: 7 targets
  main.o    <- main.c shape.h vec.h       cc -DWITH_PLOT -O2 -Wall -c main.c -o main.o
  report.o  <- report.c vec.h             cc -DWITH_PLOT -O2 -Wall -c report.c -o report.o
  vec.o     <- vec.c vec.h                cc -DWITH_PLOT -O2 -Wall -c vec.c -o vec.o
  shape.o   <- shape.c shape.h vec.h      cc -DWITH_PLOT -O2 -Wall -c shape.c -o shape.o
  plot.o    <- plot.c shape.h vec.h       cc -DWITH_PLOT -O2 -Wall -c plot.c -o plot.o
  libgeom.a <- vec.o shape.o plot.o       ar rcs libgeom.a vec.o shape.o plot.o
  demo      <- main.o report.o libgeom.a  cc -o demo main.o report.o libgeom.a
waves: [main.o report.o vec.o shape.o plot.o] [libgeom.a] [demo]
cc -DWITH_PLOT -O2 -Wall -c main.c -o main.o
cc -DWITH_PLOT -O2 -Wall -c report.c -o report.o
cc -DWITH_PLOT -O2 -Wall -c vec.c -o vec.o
cc -DWITH_PLOT -O2 -Wall -c shape.c -o shape.o
cc -DWITH_PLOT -O2 -Wall -c plot.c -o plot.o
ar rcs libgeom.a vec.o shape.o plot.o
cc -o demo main.o report.o libgeom.a
% plot/demo
c = (0, 3)
area = 6
plot: (0,0) (4,0) (0,3)

6. a second rule with a recipe for main.o: the ambiguity lint
% python make.py -C project -f Makefile_ambiguous.curry
ambiguous: main.o has 2 rules
  main.o <- main.c  $(CC) $(CPPFLAGS) $(CFLAGS) -c $< -o $@
  main.o <- main.c  $(CC) -O3 -c $< -o $@
refused: the build does not start
exit status 2

7. CFLAGS defined twice: two values, two recipes, the recipe lint
% python make.py -C project -f Makefile_twice.curry
main.o has 2 recipes
  cc  -O2 -Wall -c main.c -o main.o
  cc  -O2 -Wall -g -c main.c -o main.o
report.o has 2 recipes
  cc  -O2 -Wall -c report.c -o report.o
  cc  -O2 -Wall -g -c report.c -o report.o
vec.o has 2 recipes
  cc  -O2 -Wall -c vec.c -o vec.o
  cc  -O2 -Wall -g -c vec.c -o vec.o
shape.o has 2 recipes
  cc  -O2 -Wall -c shape.c -o shape.o
  cc  -O2 -Wall -g -c shape.c -o shape.o
refused: the build does not start
exit status 2

8. the compiler as a choice, CC = "gcc" ? "clang": two answers, and the command line decides
% python make.py -C project -f Makefile_toolchain.curry -n
main.o has 2 recipes
  clang  -O2 -Wall -c main.c -o main.o
  gcc  -O2 -Wall -c main.c -o main.o
report.o has 2 recipes
  clang  -O2 -Wall -c report.c -o report.o
  gcc  -O2 -Wall -c report.c -o report.o
vec.o has 2 recipes
  clang  -O2 -Wall -c vec.c -o vec.o
  gcc  -O2 -Wall -c vec.c -o vec.o
shape.o has 2 recipes
  clang  -O2 -Wall -c shape.c -o shape.o
  gcc  -O2 -Wall -c shape.c -o shape.o
demo has 2 recipes
  clang -o demo main.o report.o libgeom.a
  gcc -o demo main.o report.o libgeom.a
refused: the build does not start
exit status 2
% python make.py -C fresh -f Makefile_toolchain.curry CC=clang -n
plan: 6 targets
  main.o    <- main.c shape.h vec.h       clang  -O2 -Wall -c main.c -o main.o
  report.o  <- report.c vec.h             clang  -O2 -Wall -c report.c -o report.o
  vec.o     <- vec.c vec.h                clang  -O2 -Wall -c vec.c -o vec.o
  shape.o   <- shape.c shape.h vec.h      clang  -O2 -Wall -c shape.c -o shape.o
  libgeom.a <- vec.o shape.o              ar rcs libgeom.a vec.o shape.o
  demo      <- main.o report.o libgeom.a  clang -o demo main.o report.o libgeom.a
waves: [main.o report.o vec.o shape.o] [libgeom.a] [demo]

9. a rule that closes a cycle: the plan has no value
% python make.py -C fresh -f Makefile_cycle.curry -n
plan: no value (the rules have a cycle)
exit status 2

10. a source that is missing: no rule to make it
% python make.py -C incomplete
no rule to make vec.c, needed by vec.o
refused: the build does not start
exit status 2
